WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:06.070
Deer waved to the birds and they flew off.

2
00:00:06.071 --> 00:00:10.007
"Where are they going?" Beauty cried.

3
00:00:10.008 --> 00:00:12.747
"We need their help!"

4
00:00:12.748 --> 00:00:16.045
Deer stomped one foot.

5
00:00:16.046 --> 00:00:20.601
"Yes, of course I trust you," Beauty said.

6
00:00:20.602 --> 00:00:23.530
Deer looked out the window.

7
00:00:23.531 --> 00:00:26.207
Beauty did too.

8
00:00:26.208 --> 00:00:29.340
The sky was turning dark.

9
00:00:29.341 --> 00:00:32.777
Then she heard a soft noise.

10
00:00:32.778 --> 00:00:36.835
Plink! Another petal fell.

11
00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:40.501
"Oh no!" Beauty said.

12
00:00:40.502 --> 00:00:43.673
"What's happening?"

13
00:00:43.674 --> 00:00:46.751
Deer dashed out of the room.

14
00:00:46.752 --> 00:00:51.509
Beauty followed her outside.

15
00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:56.409
They ran into the garden.

16
00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.643
The woodcutters stood there.

17
00:00:59.644 --> 00:01:03.884
Above them the sky looked black.

18
00:01:03.885 --> 00:01:07.520
"A storm!" Beauty thought.

19
00:01:07.521 --> 00:01:10.734
Then she realized something.

20
00:01:10.735 --> 00:01:14.446
"Those aren't clouds," she thought.

21
00:01:14.447 --> 00:01:18.815
"It's the birds—hundreds of them!"

22
00:01:18.816 --> 00:01:22.626
The birds gathered above the woodcutters.

23
00:01:22.627 --> 00:01:26.447
They flapped their wings and dived low.

24
00:01:26.448 --> 00:01:30.758
"What's happening?" someone yelled.

25
00:01:30.759 --> 00:01:35.133
"Help! The birds are attacking!"

26
00:01:35.134 --> 00:01:38.175
The men batted at the birds.

27
00:01:38.176 --> 00:01:41.450
They tried swinging their axes.

28
00:01:41.451 --> 00:01:44.612
The birds dived and swooped.

29
00:01:44.613 --> 00:01:55.342
"Run!" the woodcutters cried. "Run!"

30
00:01:55.343 --> 00:01:59.023
The woodcutters ran out of the forest.

31
00:01:59.024 --> 00:02:05.772
Beauty cheered. "The castle is saved!"

32
00:02:05.773 --> 00:02:10.887
She spun toward Deer. "Will Beast be okay now?"

33
00:02:10.888 --> 00:02:13.322
Deer shook her head.

34
00:02:13.323 --> 00:02:20.432
"No, no!" Beauty raced back inside.

35
00:02:20.433 --> 00:02:24.675
The last petal on the rose was about to fall.

36
00:02:24.676 --> 00:02:27.924
She rushed to Beast's side.

37
00:02:27.925 --> 00:02:31.322
Beast lay lifeless in his bed.

38
00:02:31.323 --> 00:02:36.232
"Please, Beast, wake up!" she said.

39
00:02:36.233 --> 00:02:38.879
"I know your heart is broken.

40
00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.741
But it can be mended."

41
00:02:41.742 --> 00:02:46.789
She held tightly to Beast's hand.

42
00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:53.205
"You showed me that love can be fierce," she said.

43
00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:57.637
"It can also be tender."

44
00:02:57.638 --> 00:03:02.485
Beauty's heart felt like it would burst.

45
00:03:02.486 --> 00:03:05.376
"Beast, I love you!"

46
00:03:05.377 --> 00:03:10.429
Beauty softly sobbed.

47
00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:17.167
A warm breeze blew in.

48
00:03:17.168 --> 00:03:21.115
Then birds began to sing.

49
00:03:21.116 --> 00:03:26.929
And Beast's eyes opened.

